1
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,057
Asada...

2
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:25,297
Shino Asada...

3
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,237
Thank

4
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:34,320
you.

5
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,060
How do you feel?

6
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:02,500
When you're hurt, you'll
find a regretful feeling.

7
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:05,481
How do you feel?

8
00:01:07,380 --> 00:01:08,997
A painless pain.

9
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:13,157
I know that the strong strength will be?

10
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,360
Oh

11
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,428
We'll pay you back, though.

12
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:21,130
Ten thousand?

13
00:02:21,213 --> 00:02:23,139
I don't have that much money on me.

14
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,240
Well, go withdraw it, then.

15
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:31,020
No. Huh?

16
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,020
You heard.

17
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:34,460
I said no.

18
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,720
I'm not giving you guys any money.

19
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,537
You bitch.

20
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:41,420
We'll do this the hard way.

21
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,358
Get out of the way.

22
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:44,370
I want to go.

23
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:06,020
Mm-hmm.

24
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:07,930
Bang.

25
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,560
Poor Asada.

26
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,820
You know my big brother?

27
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,706
Well, he's got a buttload
of these model guns.

28
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:20,497
Wouldn't it be cool if
I brought some to class?

29
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:24,520
I know you like guns, especially pistols.

30
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,760
Uh-oh, someone's gonna hurl.

31
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,597
Remember when you blew
chunks in class and fainted?

32
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,915
Oh, God, that stank like ass for days.

33
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:40,677
All you have to do is give us your
money and we'll let you go home.

34
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:41,701
Don't you, Anna?

35
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,640
I mean, you look like hell.

36
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:46,590
Officer!

37
00:03:46,673 --> 00:03:48,534
The girl's getting mugged in the alley!

38
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,630
Hurry!

39
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,230
Bitch!

40
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,240
Asura, are you okay?

41
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:13,380
Yeah, I'm fine, Shinkawa.

42
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:14,841
Thanks for that.

43
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:26,120
So I heard what happened the other
day you went on quite the rampage.

44
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:30,117
Yeah but for a strategy
it was a fail I mean we

45
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,617
started the op with six
and lost four by the end.

46
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:36,477
Of it if that's the outcome of
an ambush we set up it's not

47
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:40,037
much of a win you know you
were pretty Rad though you know

48
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:43,137
that behemoth guy with the
minigun he was kind of a legend in

49
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:45,797
the game because he never bought
it in a squad fight before.

50
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:46,710
Yeah?

51
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,820
I had no idea he was that good.

52
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,160
I never really saw his
rankings in B .O .B.

53
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,993
His days were numbered.

54
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:56,337
I mean, no matter how
powerful a minigun is?

55
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:57,857
Carrying 500 rounds of ammo.

56
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:00,677
pushes you over the weight
limit so you can't run.

57
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:03,077
And since B .O .B.'s a
solo encounter battle,

58
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,689
he was easy pickings
for a sniper like you.

59
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:12,277
Still, with that gun, he's pretty much
invincible as long as he's with a good squad.

60
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,100
The minigun should be banned.

61
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:17,037
If we're talking about banning weapons,

62
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:20,473
don't forget, some people
think my Hecate's a cheat, too.

63
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:25,052
As its owner, I have to admit, using
it does have its own special problems.

64
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,725
Wish I had problems like that.

65
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:33,097
So, what are your plans
for the next B .O .B.?

66
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:34,780
I'm definitely entering.

67
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:39,477
I did my homework and have most of the info
of the top 20 players from the last one.

68
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,520
And I've got my Hecate now.

69
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,408
With her in my hands,
I'm sure I can kill...

70
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,420
I mean, crack the higher ranks.

71
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:54,220
If I can take out all my enemies and
prove I'm the strongest, I'll be free.

72
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:56,790
Anne.

73
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,520
Asada, you're amazing.

74
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,116
Having that awesome gun is one thing.

75
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,117
But you were also smart enough to put your

76
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,737
points on strength stats
so you could use it.

77
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:09,120
I'm the one who got you into GGO.

78
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,277
but I've been totally left behind.

79
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,580
That is so not true.

80
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:17,411
In the last qualifier, you made it all
the way to the semi-finals, remember?

81
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,170
Whatever.

82
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:22,140
An AGI build only gets you so far in GGO.

83
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,720
A good gun helps too.

84
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,160
I spent points on the wrong stat.

85
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,557
Don't get so down about that stuff.

86
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,470
Sign up for B .O .B.

87
00:06:29,553 --> 00:06:30,715
and see what happens.

88
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,740
Nah, no point. I just die.

89
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:35,910
Oh, hmm.

90
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:38,754
Hey, how are your studies coming along?

91
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,617
You still want to be a doctor?

92
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,800
Yeah, it is the family business.

93
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:46,689
I promised my dad I'd go to med
school, so it's a done deal.

94
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:47,839
Stuck with it now.

95
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,780
Well, what about cram school and the GED?

96
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,435
Are those going okay?

97
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:53,840
Oh, yeah.

98
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,240
It's going great.

99
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,677
I'm maintaining the same rank
I had when I was at school.

100
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,017
Staying sharp, ma 'am.

101
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,159
Locked and loaded.

102
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:02,410
Roger that.

103
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:09,337
The reason I asked is because
you're always online when I log on.

104
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:10,957
That's why I was a little worried.

105
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,637
If you're online that
much, when do you study?

106
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:17,896
I do most of my studying during the
day, and I take lots of breaks too.

107
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:22,457
You must be making tons of cash if
you're diving all the time like that.

108
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,897
I'm not making that much.

109
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:27,040
Solo hunting's impossible
for AGI Builds these days.

110
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:31,889
Oh, well, you're doing great if you're
earning enough for the connection fee.

111
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,700
Uh-oh, it's late.

112
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:37,140
Sorry, I have to get going now.

113
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:39,417
Oh, okay.

114
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,206
Hey, are you still making
dinner for yourself?

115
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:45,207
I'd love to try more of
your cooking someday.

116
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:47,450
Huh?

117
00:07:47,533 --> 00:07:48,777
Oh, sure. Okay.

118
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:51,919
It's just, I think I need
to get better at it first.

119
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,300
Thanks for the tea.

120
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:59,077
And thanks, I mean thank
you, for saving me.

121
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,460
You were pretty cool.

122
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:04,386
I wish I could always
be there to protect you.

123
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:08,440
Hey, if you want, I can
walk you home every day.

124
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,340
I mean, if you want.

125
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,760
Oh, no, no, that's okay.

126
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,440
I'll be fine.

127
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:16,858
It's the only way I'll get stronger.

128
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,300
What a day.

129
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,660
I can do this.

130
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,180
I don't remember what dad looked like.

131
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:56,080
I remember hearing he died
in a car accident, though.

132
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,640
Sometime before I turned two.

133
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:02,160
After the accident, my
mom and I left Tokyo.

134
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,678
We went to go live with her parents.

135
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:08,000
It was peaceful there for both of us.

136
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:24,720
And then, one day, that
peace was shattered.

137
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:39,637
Put the money in the bag, goddammit!

138
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,880
And don't hit the alarm, or else...

139
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,330
Mommy...

140
00:10:43,413 --> 00:10:44,822
Come on, don't just stand there!

141
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,256
Start filling it up!

142
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:47,720
Let's go, move it!

143
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,800
Okay, sure.

144
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,540
I told him not to!

145
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:05,680
You heard me!

146
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:07,140
Let's go, bitch!

147
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:09,445
Fill it up or you get it, too!

148
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:14,422
Give me the money now or
I'm gonna kill her next!

149
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,100
I swear I'll do it!

150
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:32,680
YOU LITTLE GIVE IT STUCK
YOU BRATS! LET'S GO!

151
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,360
LET'S GO OF MY GUN!

152
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:04,780
Oh, my God.

153
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,980
Oh, my God.

154
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,470
No!

155
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,300
I look awful.

156
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:51,620
Somebody.

157
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,340
Somebody. Anybody.

158
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,140
Save me.

159
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:06,880
Wait, what?

160
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,980
You're kidding, you're quitting ALO?

161
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:14,289
No, I'll just be gone
for a couple of days.

162
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:17,440
I'll convert back after that. But why?

163
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:21,900
Well, actually, it's complicated.

164
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:25,854
There's this other virtual
MMO that I need to check out.

165
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:27,660
Need to, huh?

166
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,637
You've done this before
and just used new accounts.

167
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:32,249
Why not for this one, too?

168
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:35,302
I mean, if you convert,
your items will be reset.

169
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,365
Why would you want to do that?

170
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:41,420
Well, it's like a favor for
that guy from the government.

171
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:50,517
I guess if Mr.

172
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:53,071
Kikuoka is asking you
to, you can't say no.

173
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,794
I don't know what it is about that man.

174
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:59,724
But there's a part of me that
still has a hard time trusting him.

175
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:02,700
Yeah, I'm not too sure
I can trust him either.

176
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:06,121
Just get back as soon as you can!

177
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:09,759
This is our home, and it's
not the same without you.

178
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:23,657
Don't worry, I'll be back
in ALO before you know it.

179
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:26,717
I'll just dive into Gun Gale
online for a couple days,

180
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,976
see what's going on, and that's that.

181
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:34,420
I'm 99 % sure the Death
Gun story's a hoax.

182
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,209
Probably someone trolling.

183
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:40,262
You can't kill someone in the real
world from the virtual anymore.

184
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:42,460
I know that's impossible.

185
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,480
This is real power, real strength.

186
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:50,880
Let your fear carve one
name into your brains.

187
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:54,940
The name I share with
this weapon, Death Gun.

188
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:01,440
But there's still that 1
% chance it could be true.

189
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,140
That's why I'm here.

190
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,260
Hello, anyone here? Yep.

191
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:16,700
What's going on, Kirigaya?

192
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:20,570
Ms.

193
00:16:20,653 --> 00:16:22,680
Aki, it's nice to see you again.

194
00:16:24,920 --> 00:16:28,620
Holy - Whoa, you finally
got some meat on you.

195
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,737
You could use some filling out, though.

196
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:32,157
You sure you're eating right?

197
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:33,946
Yeah, I'm eating, I'm eating.

198
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,534
Wait a minute, what are you doing here?

199
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:39,997
Your friend in the suit and
glasses told me about your mission.

200
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,637
He said something about
you going into a virtual

201
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:45,497
network and doing some
reconnaissance or something.

202
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,286
I can't believe he'd ask you.

203
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:49,517
I mean, you've only been back for a year.

204
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:53,397
Anyway, he found out I was the one
who was in charge of your rehab.

205
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:56,537
So he asked me to keep an eye
on your monitors while you dive.

206
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:58,877
They took me off my normal
shift and everything.

207
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:01,897
The head nurse wasn't happy,
but what can she do about it?

208
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,857
If the government wants
something, they're gonna get it.

209
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:08,116
Well, I guess you and me are
back together again, huh?

210
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,540
Yeah, thanks for being here.

211
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:16,120
So it's just us today,
no Ki-Kuoka? Mm-hmm.

212
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:18,971
He asked me to give you a message, though.

213
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,786
Email your reports to
me at the usual address.

214
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:31,237
Your fee and expenses will be
paid when you finish the mission,

215
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,967
so please don't forget
to send me an invoice.

216
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:35,570
P .S.

217
00:17:35,653 --> 00:17:38,557
Just because you're alone with a pretty
nurse, you're still on the clock.

218
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:41,581
Try to keep those hormones
of yours under control.

219
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:48,980
Uh, if it's okay, I'd like to
connect to the network now.

220
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:50,460
Yeah, sure.

221
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,900
It's all set up.

222
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:01,780
Okay, hot stuff. Strip! Why?

223
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,358
For the electrodes.

224
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,280
Oh, don't be shy.

225
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:07,660
I've seen all your goodies before.

226
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:10,680
Actually, can I just take off my shirt?

227
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,790
Mm-hmm.

228
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,270
There.

229
00:18:20,353 --> 00:18:21,299
You're good to go.

230
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,080
Well, here I go.

231
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:29,360
Wish me luck.

232
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:33,134
I don't see this taking me
more than four or five hours.

233
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,280
You got it.

234
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:37,237
And don't you worry about
your body while you're gone.

235
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:39,960
I'll keep a close eye on it. Thanks.

236
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,494
I feel better already.

237
00:18:49,580 --> 00:18:50,500
Link, start!

238
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,520
Yeah, I'm doing great.

239
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,449
I'm used to the school now, and
I've made some friends, too.

240
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:05,280
I'm fine, really.

241
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:08,822
I've only had a couple
panic attacks, that's all.

242
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,460
Yeah, Grandpa, I will.

243
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,360
Don't you catch any colds, either.

244
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:16,757
I'll come home for winter break.

245
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:18,560
Me too. Bye.

246
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:27,920
Ever since that day, whenever
I see a gun, I freak out.

247
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:33,460
If I see a picture of one, or see one
on TV, I'm guaranteed a panic attack.

248
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,617
I came to Tokyo for high school,

249
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:39,837
thinking if I got far enough
away from home, it'd help.

250
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,140
But it didn't.

251
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:45,960
One day,

252
00:19:46,400 --> 00:19:48,657
Shinkawa told me about Gun Gale Online,

253
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:52,034
and I thought it could work
as a kind of therapy for me.

254
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:54,580
And in a way, it worked.

255
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:59,300
As Sinon, when I'm holding a gun or
when someone's drawing down on me,

256
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:00,780
I can handle it.

257
